From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NixOS module overlay <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Drop the mapping type from fulltext search for OpenSearch

Zotero_FullText::searchInLibrary asks the Elasticsearch client for a
typed search:

    'index' => self::$elasticsearchType . "_index",
    'type'  => self::$elasticsearchType,

which the client turns into POST /item_fulltext_index/item_fulltext/_search.

Mapping types were deprecated in Elasticsearch 7 and removed in
Elasticsearch 8 / OpenSearch 2. Against OpenSearch there is no route for
a URL with a type segment at all, so every fulltext search answers:

    {"error":"no handler found for uri
      [/item_fulltext_index/item_fulltext/_search] and method [POST]"}

The dataserver logs this as an elasticsearch-php Connection.php error and
returns nothing, so search-in-library silently finds no results while
the rest of the API keeps working. It fires on every tag lookup the web
library makes, which is why it dominates the service log.

Dropping 'type' leaves POST /item_fulltext_index/_search, which is the
modern form and is what both OpenSearch and Elasticsearch 8 expect. The
index holds a single type, so nothing is lost by not naming it.

Note this only makes the query well-formed. The index must also exist:
misc/elasticsearch/bin/init creates it, and its final step issues a
typed mapping PUT that fails the same way. Fold the mapping into the
index-creation PUT before running it, or create the index by hand.
---
diff --git a/model/FullText.inc.php b/model/FullText.inc.php
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/model/FullText.inc.php
+++ b/model/FullText.inc.php
@@ -248,7 +248,10 @@
 	public static function searchInLibrary($libraryID, $searchText) {
 		$params = [
 			'index' => self::$elasticsearchType . "_index",
-			'type' => self::$elasticsearchType,
+			// Self-hosted: no 'type'. Mapping types were removed in
+			// OpenSearch 2 / Elasticsearch 8, and a typed search URL has
+			// no route there -- "no handler found for uri
+			// [/item_fulltext_index/item_fulltext/_search]".
 			'routing' => $libraryID,
 			'size' => 150,
 			"body" => [
